  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast bias when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) — model tends to overestimate prices.",
    "Adjust downward for forecasts that overshoot recent highs — especially after sentiment spikes.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction for persistent overestimation in early forecast periods (e.g., first 5–7 days).",
    "Increase downward pressure on forecasts when sentiment is positive and prices are trending downward.",
    "Lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, reduce next period’s forecast by 5–10% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term sentiment shifts — model should smooth out sentiment-driven volatility over 3–5 day windows."
  ]
